def get_slide_data() -> dict:
    return {
        'title': 'Theorem Step 2: Splitting Algorithm',
        'content': '\n# Theorem Step 2: The Decoupling Splitting\n\nSolving the full non-linear Boltzmann equation directly is computationally impossible. DSMC bypasses this by applying a **<span class="glossary-term" data-def="A numerical method that decouples complex processes (like advection and collision) by solving them sequentially over small time increments.">fractional-step splitting algorithm</span>**, decoupling motion and collisions over a small timestep $\\Delta t$:\n\n$$\\Delta t < \\tau_{\\text{collision}} \\approx \\frac{\\lambda}{\\langle v \\rangle}$$\n\n## The Split Sequence:\n1.  **<span class="glossary-term" data-def="The step in the splitting scheme where particles are moved along straight lines according to their velocities, ignoring collisions.">Advection Phase</span> (Deterministic Motion):**\n    For $\\Delta t$, solve the force-free, collisionless Boltzmann equation (particles move ballistically and bounce off boundaries):\n    $$\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t} + \\mathbf{v} \\cdot \\nabla f = 0 \\quad \\implies \\quad \\mathbf{x}(t + \\Delta t) = \\mathbf{x}(t) + \\mathbf{v}(t)\\Delta t$$\n2.  **<span class="glossary-term" data-def="The step in the splitting scheme where particle velocities are modified stochastically in each grid cell to simulate collisions.">Relaxation Phase</span> (Stochastic Collisions):**\n    Evaluate the collision term in local cells, modifying only particle velocities while keeping spatial positions fixed:\n    $$\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t} = \\left(\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial t}\\right)_{\\!\\text{coll}}$$\n\n\n## Decoupling Illustration from Slide Deck:\n<div style="text-align:center; margin: 1rem 0;">\n    <img src="LaTeX/slide_images/presentation_slide-37.png" alt="Operator Splitting Illustration" style="max-width:95%; border-radius:8px; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1); box-shadow:0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);">\n</div>\n\n---\n<div style="display:flex; justify-content:space-between; margin-top:1.5rem;">\n    <a href="#" class="back-btn" style="margin-bottom:0;" onclick="loadTheoremSlide(3)">&larr; Step 1</a>\n    <a href="#" class="back-btn" style="margin-bottom:0; background:rgba(16,185,129,0.15); border-color:rgba(16,185,129,0.3); color:#a7f3d0;" onclick="loadTheoremSlide(5)">Step 3: Discretization &rarr;</a>\n</div>\n'
    }
